9. SQL Queries – Sub-Queries
9.1 Students with CGPA greater than the average CGPA
SELECT student_id, student_name, cgpa
FROM Student
WHERE cgpa > (SELECT AVG(cgpa) FROM Student);
Expected result:
student_id	student_name	cgpa
101	Anu	8.70
103	Charan	8.20
104	Divya	9.10

9.2 Students belonging to the CSE department using a sub-query
SELECT student_id, student_name
FROM Student
WHERE dept_id = (
    SELECT dept_id
    FROM Department
    WHERE dept_name = 'CSE'
);
Expected result:
student_id	student_name
101	Anu
102	Bala

9.3 Students enrolled in the DBMS course
SELECT student_id, student_name
FROM Student
WHERE student_id IN (
    SELECT student_id
    FROM Enrollment
    WHERE course_id = (
        SELECT course_id
        FROM Course
        WHERE course_name = 'DBMS'
    )
);
Expected result:
student_id	student_name
101	Anu
102	Bala

9.4 Courses whose credits are greater than at least one course in the ECE department
SELECT course_id, course_name, credits
FROM Course
WHERE credits > ANY (
    SELECT credits
    FROM Course
    WHERE dept_id = 20
);
Expected result:
course_id	course_name	credits
501	DBMS	4
502	Data Structures	4

9.5 Correlated sub-query: students whose CGPA is above their department average
SELECT s.student_id, s.student_name, s.dept_id, s.cgpa
FROM Student s
WHERE s.cgpa > (
    SELECT AVG(s2.cgpa)
    FROM Student s2
    WHERE s2.dept_id = s.dept_id
);
Expected result:
student_id	student_name	dept_id	cgpa
101	Anu	10	8.70

9.6 Find the student(s) with the highest CGPA
SELECT student_id, student_name, cgpa
FROM Student
WHERE cgpa = (SELECT MAX(cgpa) FROM Student);
Expected result:
student_id	student_name	cgpa
104	Divya	9.10

10. JOIN vs Sub-Query – Quick Comparison
Feature	JOIN	Sub-Query
Basic purpose	Combines related rows from tables	Uses result of one query inside another
Typical use	Retrieving related columns	Filtering based on aggregate or another query
Example	Student JOIN Department	CGPA > AVG(CGPA)
Readability	Often clear for relationship-based retrieval	Useful when logic naturally has nested steps
